  "method": [
    "Compare previous PR head e7674bc690 against the final recorded production sources. Baseline production is unchanged; baseline and candidate have identical expanded benchmark fixtures and counter instrumentation.",
    "Frozen binaries prevent provenance mixing. Alternate baseline/candidate execution order. Document fixtures include in-process warmup and validate exact output strings, checksums, and zero retained diagnostic allocations. Setup is excluded.",
    "Document fixtures have eleven paired counted/timing runs each. Vector production timing uses eleven pairs for 20k durable retries and seven pairs for 20k mixed retries / 5k fresh ingest, all at 1536 dimensions, with group commit separately disabled and enabled.",
    "Each vector variant gets a fresh directory; retry/mixed setup is performed with the baseline binary outside the timer. Background checkpoint is disabled. Expected prepared-payload counts and complete reference-array checksums match between variants.",
    "Vector counted runs use one pair per fixture/setting as diagnostics, separate from production smp allocator timing. Document counted runs also use the diagnostic C allocator rather than the production allocator.",
    "allocations counts successful raw alloc calls only. resize_calls and remap_calls count attempted calls, including refusals. moving_remaps counts successful pointer changes; moved_bytes sums the requested new sizes of those moves.",
    "allocated_bytes is cumulative successful logical requested-storage growth. live/peak are caller-visible requested storage, not allocator overhead, transient backend realloc overlap, RSS, or complete physical allocation costs. Reporting serialization is excluded from vector counter snapshots.",
    "Timing statistics are paired medians with deterministic 10,000-resample bootstrap 95% intervals, seed 9713. Intervals spanning zero do not establish equivalence or universal zero runtime cost.",
    "Artifact-only dense/sparse replay bypasses the document-filter sets when no documents exist. Selected real dense/sparse artifact replay and corrupt-artifact integration tests pass; no separate throughput claim is made for that shortcut.",
    "Direct JSON writing preserves std.json.fmt escaping and output-list ownership on success and allocation failure. Tests cover empty/plain/quoted/control/Unicode/large strings and prove the pre-reserved path works with an allocator refusing every allocation.",
    "Durable retry eligibility validates identity/dimensions/exact-representation metadata under the pinned Opened lease. Retry success no longer checksums existing payload bytes; it is not a payload integrity scrub. Actual reads and GC copies still check payload/residual CRCs and reject corruption. Both float32 and float16-residual corruption, wrong dimensions, group settings, and unchanged retry WAL are covered.",
    "Prior full-text repair integration failure remains unresolved; these focused gates are not a complete integration run. Prior main-baseline timing uncertainty is not automatically replaced by this comparison against the previous PR head.",
    "Vector counter snapshots cover the run, final checkpoint, and reference sidecar write; initial open/setup and reporting are excluded. run_ns and final_checkpoint_ns are separate timings."
  ]
